.TH IPA-MGR 1 "2024-01-01" "freeipa-manager 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ipa-mgr \- command-line interface for FreeIPA server management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ipa-mgr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ipa-mgr
is a command-line tool for managing FreeIPA identity management servers.
It communicates with the FreeIPA JSON-RPC API and supports both Kerberos
(GSSAPI) and password-based authentication.
.PP
A companion GTK4/Adwaita graphical interface is also available as
.BR freeipa-manager (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server " " \fIHOSTNAME\fR
FreeIPA server hostname (required).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-realm " " \fIREALM\fR
Kerberos realm.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSERNAME\fR
Username for password authentication. If omitted, Kerberos authentication
is used.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASSWORD\fR
Password for password authentication. If omitted, the user is prompted
interactively.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output results in JSON format for scripting.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output (headers, counts, separators).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-verify
Disable SSL certificate verification.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B connect
Test the connection to a FreeIPA server and list available servers.
.TP
.B users \fR[\fIlist\fR|\fIshow \fILOGIN\fR]
List all users or show details for a specific user.
.TP
.B groups
List all groups.
.TP
.B hosts
List all registered hosts.
.TP
.B certs \fR[\fIlist\fR|\fIexpiring\fR] [\fB\-\-days\fR \fIN\fR]
List certificates or show those expiring within N days (default: 30).
.TP
.B policies \fR[\fB\-\-type\fR \fIhbac\fR|\fIsudo\fR]
List HBAC or sudo rules.
.TP
.B dns \fR[\fIzones\fR|\fIrecords\fR] [\fB\-\-zone\fR \fIZONE\fR]
List DNS zones or records for a specific zone.
.TP
.B status
Display a dashboard-style status summary including user, host, group,
and server counts.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error (API failure, connection error, etc.).
.TP
.B 2
Authentication failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Test connection using Kerberos:
.RS
.B ipa-mgr \-s ipa.example.com connect
.RE
.PP
List all users in JSON format:
.RS
.B ipa-mgr \-s ipa.example.com \-\-json users list
.RE
.PP
Show a specific user:
.RS
.B ipa-mgr \-s ipa.example.com users show admin
.RE
.PP
List certificates expiring within 60 days:
.RS
.B ipa-mgr \-s ipa.example.com certs expiring \-\-days 60
.RE
.PP
Authenticate with password:
.RS
.B ipa-mgr \-s ipa.example.com \-u admin \-p secret users list
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRB5CCNAME
Kerberos credential cache path, used for GSSAPI authentication.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/freeipa-manager/config.json
User configuration file storing last server, auth method, etc.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR freeipa-manager (1),
.BR ipa (1),
.BR kinit (1),
.BR klist (1)
